---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Studio Manual">
  <main class="manual">
    <h1>Welcome to Shop Sachie</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      No algorithms, no Marketplace lowballers, no monthly fees. Just a home for your sculptures, 
      dolls, paintings, and furniture flips. Here is how to run the whole thing from your phone or laptop.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Posting Something New (The 60-Second Flow)</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open your bookmark to <strong>app.pagescms.org</strong> and sign in with GitHub.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Art, Dolls & Furniture</strong> on the left, then hit <strong>New Entry</strong>.</li>
        <li>Drop in your photos straight from your camera roll.</li>
        <li>
          Pick a <strong>Status</strong>—this automatically sorts your site for you:
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Available:</strong> Goes straight to <em>The Showroom</em> with a price tag and inquiry/buy button.</li>
            <li><strong>Sold:</strong> Moves to <em>Oddities & Archive</em> with a "Sold" stamp so people can still admire your work.</li>
            <li><strong>WIP:</strong> Lands on <em>The Workbench</em>—perfect for half-finished dolls, paint tests, and thrift store "before" pics.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Hit <strong>Save</strong>. Give it ~45 seconds to bake, then refresh your live site!</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. You Just Sold a Piece—Now What?</h2>
      <p>
        Don't delete it! Open that piece in your editor, switch the <strong>Status</strong> dropdown 
        from <em>Available</em> to <em>Sold</em>, and hit <strong>Save</strong>. Your portfolio keeps 
        growing every time you make a sale.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Changing the Colors, Banner & Bio</h2>
      <p>
        Want to announce a weekend pop-up or switch the gallery wall color? Click 
        <strong>Site Vibe & Bio Settings</strong> in your dashboard:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Top Ticker Banner:</strong> Change the scrolling message at the top of the page anytime.</li>
        <li><strong>Accent & Wall Colors:</strong> Paste any hex code (e.g., <code>#ff4d00</code> for safety orange or <code>#141414</code> for dark gallery mode) and hit Save.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. It's 100% Yours</h2>
      <p>
        Every photo and note you upload lives in clean folders inside your own GitHub account. 
        If you ever want to add a custom domain name (like <code>shopsachie.com</code>) or redesign the 
        whole layout later, you own every single file.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .manual { max-width: 680px; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; opacity: 0.85; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  code { background: rgba(128,128,128,0.15); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; }
</style>
